## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design scalable, tenant-aware incident response and degradation at scale. It tests how candidates balance automated safeguards with precise human oversight and how runbooks integrate metrics, backfills, and recovery verification.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region, multi-tenant SLAs
- Degradation strategies and traffic shaping
- Cache strategy and data consistency during outages
- Canary testing, rollback criteria, post-incident validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo per-tenant degradation switch
function route(request){
  const t = request.tenant;
  if (t.degradation === 'high') return routeToCacheOnly();
  return routeToFullPath();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate this runbook in a synthetic outage? 
- Which dashboards and alerting thresholds would you use for tenants at risk?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design per-tenant budgets, dynamic throttling, and robust rollback strategies in a multi-tenant, latency-sensitive service.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant SLOs and budgets
- Burn rate calculation and budget ledger
- Edge throttling (token bucket) and graceful degradation
- Canary rollouts and automated rollback
- Observability with per-tenant metrics and PromQL

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: update per-tenant budget on each request
function onRequest(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['tenant-id'];
  const now = Date.now();
  const budget = ledger.getBudget(tenant);
  if (budget.remaining <= 0) throttle(req, tenant);
  else { forward(req); ledger.consume(tenant, estimateCost(req)); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this system under simulated traffic bursts?
- What thresholds would you choose for alerting and auto-rollback cadence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to respond to production incidents with a concrete, beginner-friendly plan focusing on observable signals, containment, rollback, and validation under time pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Observability: latency p95, error rate, queue depth, redis/backlog metrics
- Containment: throttle concurrency, pause new work, revert patch safely
- Rollback & Validation: restore previous config, synthetic tests, end-to-end checks

## Code Example
